# No Private iOS APIs

Every API used in native iOS code must be publicly documented by Apple. Private APIs cause App Store rejection or removal.

## Forbidden Patterns

```swift
// ❌ KVC access to private properties
UIApplication.shared.value(forKey: "statusBar")
view.setValue(color, forKeyPath: "_placeholderLabel")

// ❌ Dynamic resolution of private classes / selectors
NSClassFromString("_UIBackgroundTaskQueue")
NSSelectorFromString("_privateMethod")

// ❌ Raw message dispatch
objc_msgSend(...)
dlopen(...) / dlsym(...)
```

## Correct Alternatives

| Need | ❌ Wrong | ✅ Right |
|---|---|---|
| Placeholder color | `setValue:forKeyPath:` | `attributedPlaceholder` |
| Nav bar appearance | `_UINavigationBarBackground` | `UINavigationBarAppearance` (iOS 13+) |
| Status bar style | `value(forKey: "statusBar")` | `UIStatusBarManager` |
| Device info | Private SystemConfiguration | `UIDevice` |

## AI Code Review Checklist

Before committing AI-generated native code, verify:
1. No underscore-prefixed identifiers (`_statusBar`, `_UIKeyboard`, etc.)
2. No KVC access to undocumented properties
3. Prefer public UIKit / SwiftUI APIs only
